From c5bd070772cac8d5a20b3cabb6f9df2958441a2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Twilight0 <twilight0@vivaldi.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:14:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] nouveau,va: fix VP4 teardown ordering, fence sync, M2MF
 bounds, and VA surface handling

- Set obj->parent = &drm->client in nouveau_object_subchan_new() so engine
  objects can be destroyed after their parent channel.
- Wait on active BOs and destroy the pushbuf/channel before deleting VP4
  engine subchannel objects in nouveau_vp3_decoder_destroy(),
  firmware_present(), and nvc0_screen_destroy() to avoid Fermi GPU hangs.
- Implement nouveau_vp3_decoder_fence_wait/destroy_fence and export
  out_fence in nvc0_decoder_end_frame(); pass NULL to
  nouveau_pushbuf_create() for the decoder channel so its kick callback
  does not corrupt the 3D screen fence sequence.
- Guard _nouveau_fence_update() in nouveau_pushbuf_cb() to only fire for
  the screen channel and promote EMITTED fences to FLUSHED even when
  sequence_ack == sequence.
- Clamp nvc0_m2mf_transfer_rect() dimensions defensively to avoid
  XY_OUT_OF_BOUNDS hardware faults.
- Fix VA-API interlaced surface sizing, upload clamping, surface interlaced
  flag propagation, and H.264 decoder recreation when num_ref_frames exceeds
  max_references.
